#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# operate

#% text
# `operate(p, f(x, y))` gives `p(f)(x, y)`: `p` applied to the head. `operate(p, e, n)` applies it to the head at depth `n` (`n = 2`: the head of the head), and `operate(p, e, 0)` is `p(e)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
operate(p, f(x, y))
#% output
#= p(f)(x, y)

#% cell
operate(g, f(x)(y)(z), 2)
#% output
#= g(f(x))(y)(z)

#% cell
operate(p, f(x), 0)
#% output
#= p(f(x))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `apply`, `head`, `map_at`
